    {
      "name": "ask_user",
      "title": "Ask User",
      "description": "Display an interactive questionnaire ABOVE the user's prompt bar.\n\nWHEN: you need several pieces of information from the user (interview, scoping,\npreference gathering \u2014 e.g. building a skill). Instead of asking questions in\nplain text one message at a time, call this tool ONCE with all the questions of\nthe round: the UI walks the user through them one by one (clickable options +\nfree-text field) and their combined answers arrive as the NEXT user message.\n\nAFTER the call: end your turn IMMEDIATELY with one short sentence inviting the\nuser to answer below \u2014 do NOT repeat the questions in text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "questions": {
            "description": "1 to 8 questions, each {\"q\": \"question text\", \"options\": [\"suggested choice\", \u2026] (may be empty = free-text answer), \"multi\": true if several choices are valid}. The user ALWAYS gets a free-text field on top of the options. Write questions and options in the user's language. Anything past these bounds is dropped before display (max 12 options per question, 300 chars per question, 120 per option) \u2014 the result then carries a `warning` saying what was left out.",
            "items": {},
            "type": "array"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "questions"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "result": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "description": "Result of ask_user \u2014 interactive questionnaire displayed above the user's prompt bar.",
                "properties": {
                  "ok": {
                    "const": true,
                    "default": true,
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "displayed": {
                    "default": true,
                    "description": "The questionnaire panel was shown to the user.",
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "count": {
                    "description": "Number of questions displayed.",
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  "note": {
                    "description": "How the model must end its turn (do not repeat the questions).",
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "warning": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "Set when the input was clipped (extra questions/options dropped, long text cut) \u2014 tell the user what was left out."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "count",
                  "note"
                ],
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "description": "Typed shape of the error envelope produced by ``_toolkit.err()``.\n\nMirrors the error contract the chat frontend parses :\n  * ``ok`` is the discriminator (False = failure),\n  * ``error`` is a stable machine code (snake_case),\n  * ``message`` is the human-readable text,\n  * ``fix`` is an optional hint how to recover.\n\nTools declare their return type as ``Union[<SuccessModel>,\nErrEnvelope]`` so FastMCP generates a discriminated union schema\nthe LLM can pattern-match on the ``ok`` field. The runtime\nwire format is unchanged \u2014 both branches serialise to the same\nJSON dict the frontend already reads.\n\n``extra='allow'`` because ``err()`` lets each call site attach\ncontext (``cmd``, ``path``, ``expected``, ``actual``, \u2026) \u2014 these\nare kept for the LLM but aren't part of the strict schema.",
                "properties": {
                  "ok": {
                    "const": false,
                    "default": false,
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "error": {
                    "description": "Stable machine code (e.g. 'not_found', 'too_large').",
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "message": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "Human-readable error message."
                  },
                  "fix": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "Suggested recovery action."
                  },
                  "next_action": {
